# 3. SYSTEM USERS AND AUTHORIZATION

The system has three initial roles.

These are the only approved initial roles:

1. RSS Coordinator
2. Student
3. Section Representative

Do not automatically create another role, such as Super Admin, Administrator, Department Head, or Faculty, without approval.

## 3.1 RSS Coordinator

The RSS Coordinator is the primary operational authority of the RSS system.

The Coordinator is responsible for managing the RSS process and approving important activities.

### Coordinator permissions

The Coordinator can:

- Access the Coordinator dashboard.
- Review student registrations.
- Approve or reject student registrations.
- View and manage student records.
- Manage colleges, programs, year levels, academic years, and sections.
- Manage task categories.
- Create tasks.
- Edit tasks.
- Publish tasks.
- Cancel and archive tasks.
- Select target sections.
- Select individual target students.
- Manage task sessions.
- View student applications.
- Approve or reject applications.
- Record application-review remarks.
- Manage attendance records.
- Verify attendance.
- Reject invalid attendance.
- Verify service hours.
- Review hour-adjustment requests.
- Approve or reject hour adjustments.
- Review student accomplishment submissions.
- Approve accomplishments.
- Request accomplishment revisions.
- Reject accomplishment submissions.
- View submission history and evidence.
- Upload and manage official RSS templates.
- Generate individual RSS reports.
- Generate section RSS reports.
- View notifications.
- Review relevant audit logs.
- Manage authorized system records.

The Coordinator is the primary authority for approving student registration, task applications, official attendance hours, accomplishment submissions, and official reports.

### Coordinator authorization restrictions

- Only an authorized Coordinator can perform Coordinator functions.
- Students cannot perform Coordinator operations.
- Section Representatives cannot automatically access Coordinator functions.
- Coordinator decisions must be recorded.
- Sensitive actions must be auditable.

## 3.2 Student

Students use the system to participate in RSS activities and monitor their service progress.

### Student permissions

Students can:

- Register an account.
- Verify their email if email verification is enabled.
- View account approval status.
- Log in after account activation.
- View their own profile.
- View their academic information.
- View available tasks for which they are eligible.
- View task descriptions and schedules.
- Apply for tasks.
- Monitor application status.
- Withdraw applications where permitted.
- View approved activities.
- View their attendance records.
- View verified service hours.
- View service-hour adjustment results.
- Create accomplishment submissions.
- Upload supporting photographs.
- Add evidence captions.
- Submit accomplishments for review.
- View Coordinator remarks.
- Resubmit revised accomplishments.
- View previous submission versions.
- View accomplishment approval status.
- View their RSS progress.
- View or download authorized individual reports.
- Receive notifications.

### Student restrictions

Students cannot:

- Approve their own registration.
- Approve their own applications.
- Verify their own attendance.
- Credit their own service hours.
- Approve their own accomplishments.
- Modify Coordinator decisions.
- View private records belonging to other students.
- Access restricted administrative features.
- Generate official reports unless the Coordinator-authorized workflow permits it.

Students must only access records they are authorized to view.

## 3.3 Section Representative

Section Representatives assist with section-level coordination.

Potential functions include:

- View authorized section information.
- View announcements and task information.
- Assist with communication.
- View limited section participation summaries.
- Monitor authorized section-related information.

The exact access permissions of Section Representatives must be restricted.

They must not automatically have access to:

- Private student contact information.
- Student passwords or credentials.
- Coordinator-only functions.
- Official attendance verification.
- Service-hour approval.
- Accomplishment approval.
- Restricted evidence files.
- Unrelated student records.

Do not assume that a Section Representative has authority to approve or reject applications, attendance, or accomplishments.

