# 4. ACCOUNT REGISTRATION AND AUTHENTICATION

Create a secure authentication and registration process.

## Student registration

Students must provide the required account and student information.

The information may include:

- Full name
- Student number
- Email address
- Password
- College
- Program
- Year level
- Section
- Contact number
- Other approved profile information

The student submits the registration.

The account initially has a pending status.

The Coordinator reviews the submitted student information.

The Coordinator can approve or reject the registration.

Only approved and active accounts can use the full student portal.

## Account statuses

Use the approved account status values:

- pending
- active
- suspended
- deactivated

Student registration status is separate and uses:

- pending
- approved
- rejected

Do not confuse registration approval with general account status.

## Authentication requirements

Implement:

- Secure login
- Logout
- Registration
- Password hashing
- Password reset
- Account status validation
- Role-based access control
- Session security
- Email verification if configured
- Protected routes
- Authorization policies
- Form validation
- Login rate limiting

Never store plaintext passwords.

Never expose password hashes or private account fields to the frontend.

