# 7. COMPLETE BUSINESS WORKFLOWS

Implement these workflows in the backend and frontend.

## Workflow A: Student registration

1. Student opens registration page.
2. Student submits information.
3. System validates data.
4. Account is created with pending account status.
5. Student registration is marked pending.
6. Coordinator receives a notification.
7. Coordinator reviews the registration.
8. Coordinator approves or rejects.
9. System records the decision and review information.
10. Approved account is activated according to the authorization rules.
11. Student is notified.
12. Rejected registration remains properly recorded.

Do not let a student approve their own registration.

## Workflow B: Task creation and publication

1. Coordinator opens task management.
2. Coordinator creates a task.
3. Coordinator selects category.
4. Coordinator chooses target college.
5. Coordinator sets visibility.
6. Coordinator sets capacity if applicable.
7. Coordinator defines application dates.
8. Coordinator defines activity dates.
9. Coordinator creates one or more sessions.
10. Coordinator assigns target sections or students when needed.
11. Coordinator saves as draft.
12. Coordinator publishes when ready.
13. System makes the task visible only to eligible users.
14. Eligible students receive notifications.

## Workflow C: Student application

1. Student opens available tasks.
2. System filters tasks based on eligibility.
3. Student opens task details.
4. Student submits application.
5. System validates application eligibility.
6. System prevents duplicate applications.
7. System checks capacity.
8. System creates pending application.
9. Coordinator receives notification.
10. Coordinator reviews the application.
11. Coordinator approves or rejects it.
12. System records the decision and remarks.
13. Student receives notification.
14. Approved student can access relevant activity information.

## Workflow D: Service attendance

1. Student has an approved application.
2. Student attends the activity.
3. Attendance is recorded against the task session.
4. System stores check-in/check-out or other authorized attendance information.
5. System calculates recorded hours when possible.
6. Attendance is marked pending verification.
7. Coordinator reviews attendance.
8. Coordinator verifies or rejects it.
9. System stores the decision, verified hours, and verifier.
10. Only verified hours become credited hours.

## Workflow E: Service-hour adjustment

1. Authorized user requests an adjustment.
2. Reason is recorded.
3. Adjustment hours are recorded.
4. Coordinator reviews.
5. Coordinator approves or rejects.
6. Decision is recorded.
7. Only approved adjustments count.
8. Student can view the result.

## Workflow F: Accomplishment submission

1. Student opens their completed service activity.
2. Student creates an accomplishment draft.
3. Student records activity date.
4. Student writes accomplishment description.
5. Student optionally adds remarks.
6. Student uploads evidence photographs.
7. Student categorizes photographs.
8. Student submits the accomplishment.
9. System creates the appropriate submission version.
10. Coordinator receives notification.
11. Coordinator reviews the submission.
12. Coordinator approves, requests revision, or rejects.
13. System records the review.

## Workflow G: Accomplishment revision

1. Coordinator requests revision.
2. Coordinator provides remarks.
3. Student receives notification.
4. Student opens the submission history.
5. Student reviews remarks.
6. Student creates a revised version.
7. System preserves the previous version.
8. Student submits the revision.
9. Coordinator reviews the new version.
10. System stores the decision and review history.

Never overwrite a historical submission.

## Workflow H: Individual RSS report

1. Coordinator opens the report module.
2. Coordinator selects student and approved accomplishment submission.
3. Coordinator selects the appropriate college template.
4. System checks the submission's approval status.
5. System creates the individual PDF.
6. System stores report metadata and file path.
7. System records the exact source submission.
8. Coordinator can review/download the report.
9. Authorized users can access the report according to permissions.

## Workflow I: Section RSS report

1. Coordinator opens the report module.
2. Coordinator selects a section.
3. Coordinator selects academic year.
4. Coordinator selects the appropriate report template.
5. System gathers eligible approved submissions.
6. System generates the consolidated PDF.
7. System creates report_items records.
8. System stores report metadata and file path.
9. Coordinator can review/download the report.
10. The report preserves which submissions were included.

