# 8. APPROVED POSTGRESQL DATABASE DESIGN — EXACTLY 28 TABLES

This is the authoritative database design.

The database must use PostgreSQL.

Do not redesign these tables just because another structure seems easier.

Do not rename approved tables.

Do not add or remove tables without approval.

Use BIGINT primary keys unless explicitly specified otherwise.

Use TIMESTAMPTZ for timestamp fields where specified.

Use PostgreSQL foreign keys, unique constraints, check constraints, and partial indexes where defined.

## TABLE 1: users

Purpose: Stores user account information.

Columns:

- id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY
- name VARCHAR(150)
- email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE
- password VARCHAR(255), securely hashed
- account_status with allowed values pending, active, suspended, deactivated
- email_verified_at TIMESTAMPTZ NULL
- remember_token
- created_at
- updated_at
- deleted_at TIMESTAMPTZ NULL

The password must never be returned through normal user-facing API responses.

## TABLE 2: roles

Purpose: Stores the system roles.

Columns:

- id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY
- name VARCHAR(50) UNIQUE
- description TEXT
- created_at
- updated_at

Initial roles:

- RSS Coordinator
- Student
- Section Representative

## TABLE 3: user_roles

Purpose: Assigns roles to users.

Columns:

- id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY
- user_id FK to users
- role_id FK to roles
- assigned_by FK to users, nullable
- assigned_at TIMESTAMPTZ

Constraint:

- UNIQUE(user_id, role_id)

## TABLE 4: colleges

Purpose: Stores college information.

Columns:

- id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY
- name VARCHAR(150)
- code VARCHAR(30) UNIQUE
- description
- is_active BOOLEAN
- created_at
- updated_at

Initial use: College of Technology.

Future expansion: Additional colleges.

## TABLE 5: programs

Purpose: Stores academic programs belonging to a college.

Columns:

- id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY
- college_id FK to colleges
- name VARCHAR(150)
- code VARCHAR(30)
- is_active BOOLEAN
- created_at
- updated_at

Constraint:

- UNIQUE(college_id, code)

## TABLE 6: year_levels

Purpose: Stores academic year-level definitions.

Columns:

- id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY
- name VARCHAR(50) UNIQUE
- sort_order SMALLINT UNIQUE

Use sort_order to control display order.

Do not replace it with an unrelated field.

## TABLE 7: academic_years

Purpose: Stores academic-year information.

Columns:

- id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY
- name VARCHAR(20) UNIQUE
- start_date DATE
- end_date DATE
- is_current BOOLEAN
- created_at
- updated_at

Constraints:

- end_date must be later than start_date.
- Only one academic year may be current.

Use a PostgreSQL partial unique index for is_current = TRUE.

## TABLE 8: sections

Purpose: Stores sections belonging to programs and year levels.

Columns:

- id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY
- program_id FK to programs
- year_level_id FK to year_levels
- name VARCHAR(50)
- is_active BOOLEAN
- created_at
- updated_at

Constraint:

- UNIQUE(program_id, year_level_id, name)

## TABLE 9: students

Purpose: Stores student profile information.

Columns:

- id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY
- user_id FK to users, UNIQUE
- student_number VARCHAR(50) UNIQUE
- first_name VARCHAR(150)
- middle_name nullable
- last_name VARCHAR(150)
- suffix nullable
- sex nullable; confirm its intended data type before implementing
- birth_date nullable
- contact_number VARCHAR(50) nullable
- registration_status with values pending, approved, rejected
- reviewed_by FK to users, nullable
- reviewed_at nullable
- created_at
- updated_at

Each student record belongs to one user account.

## TABLE 10: student_section_history

Purpose: Preserves section membership history across academic years.

Columns:

- id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY
- student_id FK to students
- section_id FK to sections
- academic_year_id FK to academic_years
- enrolled_at DATE
- ended_at DATE nullable
- is_current BOOLEAN
- created_at
- updated_at

Constraint:

- Partial unique index on student_id where is_current = TRUE.

A student must not have more than one current section record.

Historical section assignments must be preserved.

## TABLE 11: task_categories

Purpose: Classifies RSS service activities.

Columns:

- id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY
- name VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE
- description
- is_active BOOLEAN
- created_at
- updated_at

Do not invent final approved category seed data without approval.

## TABLE 12: tasks

Purpose: Main task/service activity records.

Columns:

- id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY
