  +-- Services / Business Logic
  +-- Policies
  +-- Notifications
  +-- Report Generation
  +-- File Upload Handling
  +-- Audit Logging
  |
  +--------------------+
  |                    |
  v                    v
PostgreSQL          Protected Storage
Database            Images / Templates / PDFs

## Backend requirements

Use Laravel for:

- Authentication
- Authorization
- Routing
- Controllers
- Form validation
- Eloquent models
- Database migrations or approved SQL scripts
- Services
- Transactions
- Notifications
- File storage
- PDF generation
- Error handling
- Automated tests

Use service classes for critical workflows rather than placing all business logic in controllers.

Use policies and middleware for authorization.

Do not rely only on frontend conditions to protect data.

## PostgreSQL requirements

PostgreSQL is the authoritative relational database.

Use:

- Foreign keys
- Unique constraints
- Check constraints
- Appropriate indexes
- Partial indexes
- Transactions
- Row locking where needed
- JSONB for audit values
- UUID where specified

Do not use SQLite as a substitute for PostgreSQL validation.

Do not require XAMPP.

